Dafny now builds against Boogie v3.5.5+review.5d9897bc, which states the canonical map read-over-write axiom of the arguments type encoding, for a map whose result type is a type parameter, as one axiom per native result sort and one for the other result types. This is equivalent to the single guarded axiom it replaces, but no instance case-splits over every native sort, so proofs that the canonical payloads had pushed out of resource verify again at about their former cost (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/425). `--legacy-noncanonical-map-payloads` is unchanged.
